WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.282
But the first practice I'm going to show you, we'll learn it on the seventh day.

2
00:00:03.282 --> 00:00:05.193
We're going to do a CV4.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.670
So that means we're going to do a ventricular compression of the fourth ventricle

4
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.692
because we are actually connected to Mangadi.

5
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.970
is the great explorer of all the extra-encephalic space.

6
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.660
That is to say, you have a connection at the level of your fourth ventricle with the

7
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.010
choroid plexuses that are located at the level of the ventricles,

8
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.090
for the production of your cerebrospinal fluid, and so you have at some point the

9
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.970
space here behind, where you have this opening between the intra-encephalic fluid

10
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.660
compartment, fourth ventricle, third ventricle, the eyes and the processes of the

11
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.730
lateral ventricles towards the fourth ventricle, which gives a small hole that we

12
00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.100
call the foramen of Magendie.

13
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.950
You imagine, here, I am inside the fluid.

14
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.410
And there, I arrive, and here, there is a hole.

15
00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.700
Well, there, I can get out.

16
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.880
And I enter the extra-encephalic compartment.

17
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.040
There is fluid here too.

18
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.850
You are the brain, not really. You see?

19
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.790
And so, it's a balance between this intra- and extra-encephalic.

20
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.450
And so, the eye, it's a balance between the environment,

21
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:03.940
intra and exterior of yourself.

22
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.600
And so, we are going to seek this state of balance through a CV4,

23
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.360
a compression of the fourth ventricle, until at some point,

24
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.470
there is a release for...

25
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.490
And there, you would have to be very attentive to do an EV4,

26
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:18.240
an expansion of the fourth ventricle towards my B zone to fill the space around.

27
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.130
It's a practice on its very first levels of concentration.

28
00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.550
Because what's important is to see the eye as a liquid.

29
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.910
You will adjust together.

30
00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:28.590
And this compression, at some point, you will have to do it for at least 7 minutes.

31
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.230
Until that moment, there is this inhalation phase.

32
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.860
The body, it will come out.

33
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.490
And it will have this expansion.

34
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.650
And in this expansion, I propose to you to expand it throughout the B zone.

35
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.840
So, in the space around.

36
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.640
You have to have a bit of neutrality.

37
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.600
So, don't try to do it well, so to speak.

38
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.220
If you want to start doing it well, already, you put yourself in your egoistic

39
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:46.920
competition.

40
00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.270
It's useless, it's just.

41
00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.560
Try to be neutral and let go a little bit.

42
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.860
It can go quite fast, this notion of space around us,

43
00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.940
and this notion of taking the person until they have their neutral.

44
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.840
Because it is the meeting of the two neutrals that creates a healing space.

45
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.530
Doctor Jealous, an American who still knew a little bit about the ancestors,

46
00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:04.600
had to treat Becker.

47
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.220
And so he arrives for Becker and he starts to treat,

48
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.330
and then after that, a minute, Becker says "But what do you want?

49
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.820
" you do, nothing is happening there, he tells me but I am treating you.

50
00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.380
And in fact, that's where Djalo says to himself, I understood that there,

51
00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.700
in fact, the treatment in fact began when I finished.

52
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.530
And so we go too fast.

53
00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.940
Let the process take its time to settle, let the room settle,

54
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.470
let the neutrality take its time.

55
00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.500
Often, in fact, the true biodynamic therapeutic process begins in fact when you have

56
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.620
finished your treatment.

57
00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.990
It's a grip where we take like that, so you have to visualize this CV4,

58
00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:37.630
it's behind the cerebellum, so I put myself at the level of just below the space at

59
00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.950
the level of Ignon like this, it's a hand.

60
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.200
So what I like is to see here, sometimes some people come to compress completely the

61
00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.540
carotid arteries, be careful, all of a sudden if they become all blue, we stop.

62
00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.890
So do not compress the carotid arteries, so the thumbs are slightly loose and I must

63
00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.520
try that I myself am in a good position.

64
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.390
So if I'm a bit like that, I'm implying another force,

65
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.750
you see, you feel, if I put myself like this, there.

66
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.550
And in fact, a V4 fire, it's something that is worked with your whole body.

67
00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.390
